1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,500
Everything's all set.

2
00:00:10,060 --> 00:00:12,200
I can bring down this building any time.

3
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:17,000
I'm feeling confident about my mana.

4
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:21,620
So if anything happens to the others, I can cover for them.

5
00:00:22,680 --> 00:00:24,940
This is enough, right?

6
00:00:25,820 --> 00:00:28,720
I'm using magic to knock the dragon out.

7
00:00:28,720 --> 00:00:33,280
Instead of trying to hit it directly and risk hurting the others in the crossfire,

8
00:00:33,560 --> 00:00:36,220
I'm gonna collapse a building on top of it.

9
00:00:37,140 --> 00:00:39,340
Yeah, this is the best way.

10
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:42,100
Stay calm.

11
00:00:45,480 --> 00:00:48,000
I have to focus on the job I was given.

12
00:00:49,640 --> 00:00:51,180
We'll make this work.

13
00:00:52,680 --> 00:00:54,740
Valon, just hold out for us.

14
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:52,760
It's us!

15
00:02:52,760 --> 00:02:53,620
Run!

16
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:59,700
It's fast!

17
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:03,720
Fun fact, red dragons can run up to 60 kilometers per hour!

18
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:04,700
That's fun!

19
00:03:04,940 --> 00:03:07,000
It's fine, the terrain's slowing it down!

20
00:03:08,040 --> 00:03:09,420
Up ahead, turn right!

21
00:03:16,260 --> 00:03:18,640
Now we baited fire breath down this corridor!

22
00:03:20,040 --> 00:03:23,680
Dragons store fuel in their bellies, and click their tongue to ignite it!

23
00:03:24,180 --> 00:03:25,600
For our own safety!

24
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:28,260
We have to make it exhaust all of its fuel!

25
00:03:31,080 --> 00:03:32,140
It's tonguing!

26
00:03:32,820 --> 00:03:33,820
Look out!

27
00:03:33,820 --> 00:03:39,500
Such intense heat!

28
00:03:40,160 --> 00:03:41,080
But...

29
00:03:41,080 --> 00:03:49,420
We can handle it thanks to the pan and spells!

30
00:03:49,420 --> 00:03:50,680
Yes!

31
00:03:50,680 --> 00:03:52,680
We've got the...

32
00:03:52,680 --> 00:03:55,360
Oh, no!

33
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:57,620
The heat from the pan...

34
00:03:57,620 --> 00:03:59,620
It's spreading evenly...

35
00:03:59,620 --> 00:04:01,880
Cut!

36
00:04:01,880 --> 00:04:13,600
Oh, yeah, of course it's hot!

37
00:04:14,260 --> 00:04:17,000
Since he was cooking with that pan every single day!

38
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:19,500
I assumed it would be able to repel dragon fire!

39
00:04:20,180 --> 00:04:24,140
According to Namari, adamantine is supposed to block all attacks from a dragon!

40
00:04:24,140 --> 00:04:26,140
I think she was making stuff up!

41
00:04:26,140 --> 00:04:27,140
I think she was making stuff up!

42
00:04:27,140 --> 00:04:28,140
Was not...

43
00:04:28,140 --> 00:04:33,000
Here it comes!

44
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:33,520
Damn it!

45
00:04:34,040 --> 00:04:35,060
I've got a change course!

46
00:04:35,060 --> 00:04:35,920
Let's go back!

47
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:40,640
Hmm?

48
00:04:42,140 --> 00:04:42,860
Huh?

49
00:04:43,600 --> 00:04:44,400
What?

50
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:46,000
They're here?

51
00:04:46,660 --> 00:04:47,460
Already?

52
00:04:48,520 --> 00:04:49,700
But why?

53
00:04:50,200 --> 00:04:53,040
I thought that we were supposed to stay split up!

54
00:04:53,280 --> 00:04:55,340
Should I still do things according to plan?

55
00:04:56,120 --> 00:04:57,800
Ah, fine then!

56
00:04:58,380 --> 00:04:59,980
Here I go!

57
00:05:05,060 --> 00:05:35,040
Here I go!

58
00:05:35,040 --> 00:05:37,360
Oh, my God!

59
00:05:46,400 --> 00:05:52,220
Are you kidding me?

60
00:05:52,560 --> 00:05:53,580
It didn't work!

61
00:05:54,940 --> 00:05:55,860
Quiet!

62
00:05:56,600 --> 00:05:57,860
Don't move!

63
00:05:57,860 --> 00:06:09,620
The inverse scale's right there!

64
00:06:10,260 --> 00:06:13,020
If I get a bit closer, it's mine!

65
00:06:13,020 --> 00:06:26,760
It made a run for it!

66
00:06:27,420 --> 00:06:28,520
Damn it, Tensuke!

67
00:06:28,780 --> 00:06:31,020
You're just a monster after...

68
00:06:31,020 --> 00:06:31,700
Did you?

69
00:06:31,700 --> 00:06:32,060
You two!

70
00:06:32,360 --> 00:06:32,800
Get up!

71
00:06:33,080 --> 00:06:33,360
Hurry!

72
00:06:34,200 --> 00:06:34,980
Up up us!

73
00:06:36,480 --> 00:06:37,620
Get under its belly!

74
00:06:38,280 --> 00:06:39,200
Damn you, Elias!

75
00:06:39,320 --> 00:06:40,540
Look, I'm sorry, okay?

76
00:06:41,180 --> 00:06:41,940
Damn it!

77
00:06:42,140 --> 00:06:44,540
The common language doesn't have enough curse words!

78
00:06:44,800 --> 00:06:45,240
Punza!

79
00:06:45,500 --> 00:06:45,920
Valo!

80
00:06:45,920 --> 00:06:49,320
Please, don't cuss at me in a language I don't speak, Chilchak!

81
00:06:49,900 --> 00:06:51,080
Any plans, genius?

82
00:06:53,240 --> 00:06:54,600
Look really mad!

83
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:55,520
This way!

84
00:06:55,860 --> 00:06:57,120
Let's run out the tail slide!

85
00:07:00,720 --> 00:07:02,460
On second thought, nixed that.

86
00:07:02,640 --> 00:07:05,560
This is where we live now, under the red dragon's crotch.

87
00:07:05,560 --> 00:07:09,640
No good.

88
00:07:09,940 --> 00:07:11,900
Simple spells aren't gonna work on it at all!

89
00:07:12,140 --> 00:07:12,440
Focus!

90
00:07:21,080 --> 00:07:24,220
What the hell was that?

91
00:07:24,220 --> 00:07:25,920
Did you just go and shatter our last weapon?

92
00:07:26,720 --> 00:07:28,260
How do we fix this mess?

93
00:07:28,960 --> 00:07:29,960
No choice.

94
00:07:30,660 --> 00:07:31,520
Use this.

95
00:07:32,280 --> 00:07:32,600
Huh?

96
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:35,860
Does this mean that knife is made from a special metal?

97
00:07:36,480 --> 00:07:39,200
It cuts the bones and skin of any monster.

98
00:07:39,660 --> 00:07:42,180
I've never gone a day without taking good care of it.

99
00:07:42,580 --> 00:07:44,060
It's a mithril kitchen knife.

100
00:07:44,500 --> 00:07:46,720
Maybe the only one of its kind in the world.

101
00:07:47,620 --> 00:07:48,140
Mithril?

102
00:07:48,880 --> 00:07:49,360
Seriously?

103
00:07:50,380 --> 00:07:52,100
Wish we could have shown Namaari.

104
00:07:52,420 --> 00:07:54,920
Pretty sure she would have killed Senshi if we had.

105
00:07:55,200 --> 00:07:58,260
Yeah, I had a feeling that was the case, so I kept my mouth shut.

106
00:07:58,260 --> 00:08:03,060
Take this!

107
00:08:04,100 --> 00:08:04,580
Whoa!

108
00:08:04,780 --> 00:08:06,760
It really pierced right through the scales!

109
00:08:09,760 --> 00:08:15,440
But with the size of this blade, no matter where I stabbed, I doubt I'd be able to fatally wound it.

110
00:08:15,440 --> 00:08:25,840
Oh, crap!

111
00:08:26,140 --> 00:08:26,760
What now?

112
00:08:27,100 --> 00:08:29,200
This means that the plan failed, doesn't it?

113
00:08:29,620 --> 00:08:31,800
Or is this some sort of new one?

114
00:08:32,300 --> 00:08:33,900
What the heck do I do?

115
00:08:36,900 --> 00:08:38,380
There's no time to hesitate!

116
00:08:39,020 --> 00:08:39,460
Stop!

117
00:08:39,780 --> 00:08:40,360
Get back!

118
00:08:40,360 --> 00:08:43,880
I'm getting farther from my sword.

119
00:08:44,760 --> 00:08:47,680
We're gonna end up in the town square if we keep backing up.

120
00:08:48,080 --> 00:08:49,920
And then we'll get burnt to a crisp!

121
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:51,720
I'll distract the dragon.

122
00:08:52,880 --> 00:08:54,120
No, you can't!

123
00:08:54,720 --> 00:08:57,160
Lyos, I know you know this.

124
00:08:57,860 --> 00:09:00,320
Of all the monsters that we've eaten so far,

125
00:09:00,560 --> 00:09:03,360
were there any that didn't fight until their last breath?

126
00:09:04,220 --> 00:09:05,720
It's eat or be eaten here.

127
00:09:06,040 --> 00:09:09,620
If we don't give it our all, then we're gonna be some monsters' dinner.

128
00:09:09,620 --> 00:09:11,240
Here, prepare yourself!

129
00:09:12,900 --> 00:09:13,620
Sensei!

130
00:09:25,540 --> 00:09:26,620
No, stop!

131
00:09:27,140 --> 00:09:29,100
There's no point in just running out there!

132
00:09:29,900 --> 00:09:30,760
Go find Marcel!

133
00:09:31,120 --> 00:09:32,300
You two think of a new plan!

134
00:09:33,660 --> 00:09:35,060
Hey, are you alive?

135
00:09:35,320 --> 00:09:36,140
I'll get this off!

136
00:09:36,140 --> 00:09:36,640
Huh?

137
00:09:39,620 --> 00:09:41,100
Can you move?

138
00:09:42,360 --> 00:09:55,480
I did it!

139
00:10:00,960 --> 00:10:03,360
Why is this thing stuck to the ground?

140
00:10:03,360 --> 00:10:13,220
I'll be right back!

141
00:10:14,560 --> 00:10:15,460
Come on!

142
00:10:15,840 --> 00:10:16,760
Get up!

143
00:10:17,760 --> 00:10:18,640
Sensei!

144
00:10:18,640 --> 00:10:30,980
Sorry, Marcel!

145
00:10:31,700 --> 00:10:32,820
I didn't know you were here.

146
00:10:33,080 --> 00:10:35,520
Uh, good to know that the spell is working.

147
00:10:36,360 --> 00:10:37,320
What's going on?

148
00:10:37,500 --> 00:10:38,200
Where are the others?

149
00:10:38,540 --> 00:10:39,880
It's not looking too good.

150
00:10:40,380 --> 00:10:42,040
All the plans we had set up failed.

151
00:10:42,660 --> 00:10:45,120
The other two are still out there with the dragon.

152
00:10:45,340 --> 00:10:45,620
Huh?

153
00:10:45,620 --> 00:10:47,720
What should we do?

154
00:10:48,200 --> 00:10:50,580
Does that mean we have to use my magic?

155
00:10:51,080 --> 00:10:52,800
The dragon is wounded and violent.

156
00:10:53,500 --> 00:10:55,300
It'll be too dangerous to get near it.

157
00:10:55,440 --> 00:10:57,780
But we have to do something and fast.

158
00:10:58,340 --> 00:10:59,220
Let's move upward.

159
00:10:59,640 --> 00:10:59,840
Huh?

160
00:11:00,800 --> 00:11:01,780
To do what?

161
00:11:02,180 --> 00:11:04,060
We'll get level with the dragon's face.

162
00:11:04,300 --> 00:11:05,300
And I'll get on the pan.

163
00:11:05,560 --> 00:11:06,360
The pan?

164
00:11:06,360 --> 00:11:08,860
And once I'm there, you'll blow it up.

165
00:11:09,780 --> 00:11:10,220
What?

166
00:11:12,180 --> 00:11:14,140
It's been blinded in its left eye.

167
00:11:14,500 --> 00:11:18,840
So if we approach from that side, we should be able to jump on it without being noticed.

168
00:11:19,400 --> 00:11:20,440
Are you sure?

169
00:11:21,820 --> 00:11:24,660
Marcel, you did something similar before, didn't you?

170
00:11:25,080 --> 00:11:26,320
Back when you fought the Undine.

171
00:11:27,060 --> 00:11:30,260
Yeah, but at the time, I had water walking in water.

172
00:11:30,540 --> 00:11:32,560
I have the pan and abjuration magic.

173
00:11:32,560 --> 00:11:34,140
And then what?

174
00:11:34,480 --> 00:11:37,260
How will you hit the inverse scale while clinging to its face?

175
00:11:38,280 --> 00:11:39,060
Don't worry.

176
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:40,000
I've got an idea.

177
00:11:41,340 --> 00:11:43,640
We can't make any more mistakes.

178
00:11:44,620 --> 00:11:46,160
I've no intention to.

179
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:54,560
I'm a little hesitant that this is going to work, but...

180
00:11:55,220 --> 00:11:57,140
I trust you.

181
00:11:57,140 --> 00:12:27,120
I'm a little hesitant.

182
00:12:27,140 --> 00:12:28,660
You're going to get flung off.

183
00:12:29,120 --> 00:12:30,500
Hurry and go through with the plan.

184
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:32,640
It'll be over fast.

185
00:12:33,920 --> 00:12:35,220
It's not that big a deal.

186
00:12:36,360 --> 00:12:38,060
Compared to what Valon went through.

187
00:12:38,860 --> 00:12:39,700
This is nothing!

188
00:12:43,700 --> 00:12:44,580
Lyos, no!

189
00:12:44,580 --> 00:12:44,920
No!

190
00:12:44,920 --> 00:12:44,980
No!

191
00:12:44,980 --> 00:12:50,960
No!

192
00:12:59,620 --> 00:13:00,240
No!

193
00:13:00,560 --> 00:13:00,860
No!

194
00:13:00,860 --> 00:13:01,120
No!

195
00:13:01,120 --> 00:13:01,140
Okay.

196
00:13:01,140 --> 00:13:01,340
No!

197
00:13:01,340 --> 00:13:01,920
No!

198
00:13:01,920 --> 00:13:02,980
No!

199
00:13:02,980 --> 00:13:32,960
I don't know.

200
00:13:32,980 --> 00:14:02,960
I don't know.

201
00:14:02,980 --> 00:14:32,960
I don't know.

202
00:14:32,960 --> 00:14:34,960
I don't know.

203
00:14:34,960 --> 00:14:36,960
I don't know.

204
00:14:36,960 --> 00:14:38,960
I don't know.

205
00:14:38,960 --> 00:14:40,960
Help me.

206
00:14:40,960 --> 00:14:43,260
So cold.

207
00:14:43,960 --> 00:14:45,960
Can't breathe.

208
00:14:46,960 --> 00:14:49,360
Rallin, run.

209
00:14:49,360 --> 00:14:53,360
Bios!

210
00:14:53,360 --> 00:15:01,360
Leave my brother...

211
00:15:01,360 --> 00:15:03,360
alone!

212
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:19,360
The person in that grave there...

213
00:15:19,360 --> 00:15:23,360
His ring is binding his soul here.

214
00:15:23,360 --> 00:15:25,360
Please remove it.

215
00:15:25,360 --> 00:15:27,360
The ghost will then be freed.

216
00:15:27,360 --> 00:15:29,360
His ring?

217
00:15:29,360 --> 00:15:31,360
Is this real?

218
00:15:31,360 --> 00:15:35,360
This is the grave of Oldman who died recently.

219
00:15:35,360 --> 00:15:39,360
When he was alive, he bragged about how he bought a golden ring from an elf.

220
00:15:39,360 --> 00:15:43,360
But how would a child know about that?

221
00:15:43,360 --> 00:15:47,360
Did I...

222
00:15:47,360 --> 00:15:49,360
Do something bad?

223
00:15:49,360 --> 00:15:51,360
No, you did great, Fallon.

224
00:15:51,360 --> 00:15:53,360
Ghost magic is a cool talent to have.

225
00:15:53,360 --> 00:15:55,360
Don't be sad.

226
00:15:55,360 --> 00:15:57,360
Grownups are just scared of magic.

227
00:15:57,360 --> 00:16:01,360
I think you should go and study it for real.

228
00:16:01,360 --> 00:16:03,360
It'll help you get work, you know?

229
00:16:03,360 --> 00:16:04,360
It will?

230
00:16:04,360 --> 00:16:05,360
Probably.

231
00:16:05,360 --> 00:16:07,360
You could try priest, grave keeper...

232
00:16:07,360 --> 00:16:10,360
Ooh, traveling exorcist might be fun too.

233
00:16:10,360 --> 00:16:16,360
You could wander across the lands and help people who need you.

234
00:16:16,360 --> 00:16:18,360
Wow, I like that.

235
00:16:18,360 --> 00:16:20,360
Would you be able to come with me too, brother?

236
00:16:20,360 --> 00:16:22,360
Of course.

237
00:16:22,360 --> 00:16:24,360
Where should we go first?

238
00:16:24,360 --> 00:16:25,360
Hmm...

239
00:16:25,360 --> 00:16:27,360
How about the ocean?

240
00:16:27,360 --> 00:16:29,360
Ooh, or the desert!

241
00:16:29,360 --> 00:16:30,360
I hear?

242
00:16:30,360 --> 00:16:32,360
There's a country with talking dogs there.

243
00:16:32,360 --> 00:16:34,360
Let's go, please!

244
00:16:36,360 --> 00:16:37,360
But...

245
00:16:37,360 --> 00:16:41,360
It might be best if we don't travel together anymore.

246
00:16:41,360 --> 00:16:42,360
Fallon?

247
00:16:42,360 --> 00:16:43,360
Why?

248
00:16:45,360 --> 00:16:47,360
Don't worry about me.

249
00:16:48,360 --> 00:16:51,360
Goodbye, big brother.

250
00:16:55,360 --> 00:16:56,360
Lyos, you okay?

251
00:16:57,360 --> 00:17:00,360
I stopped the bleeding for now, so hold on a bit longer.

252
00:17:00,360 --> 00:17:03,360
I'll go find the other two, along with your leg!

253
00:17:03,360 --> 00:17:08,360
Don't worry about me, huh?

254
00:17:08,360 --> 00:17:12,360
You really shouldn't say such sad things.

255
00:17:12,360 --> 00:17:14,360
I'm gonna bring you home.

256
00:17:14,360 --> 00:17:15,360
I promise.

257
00:17:16,360 --> 00:17:18,360
Hey!

258
00:17:18,360 --> 00:17:20,360
Chill, Chuck!

259
00:17:20,360 --> 00:17:22,360
Senshi!

260
00:17:25,360 --> 00:17:27,360
Thank goodness!

261
00:17:27,360 --> 00:17:28,360
You okay?

262
00:17:28,360 --> 00:17:29,360
No, you're not.

263
00:17:31,360 --> 00:17:34,360
I need more practice with my abjuration magic, huh?

264
00:17:34,360 --> 00:17:37,360
We're still mostly in one piece, so it could be worse.

265
00:17:45,360 --> 00:17:47,360
Motherfrog!

266
00:17:48,360 --> 00:17:50,360
He's suffering more than before.

267
00:17:50,360 --> 00:17:53,360
You get healing pains if you fix a big injury in a short time.

268
00:17:53,360 --> 00:17:54,360
It's fine.

269
00:17:54,360 --> 00:17:56,360
That just means it healed properly.

270
00:17:56,360 --> 00:17:58,360
Now it's your turn, Senshi!

271
00:17:58,360 --> 00:17:59,360
No, thanks.

272
00:17:59,360 --> 00:18:00,360
I'll fix it myself.

273
00:18:01,360 --> 00:18:02,360
But that'll take you months.

274
00:18:02,360 --> 00:18:04,360
Fallon was always better at healing magic,

275
00:18:04,360 --> 00:18:07,360
but I at least have the confidence of being able to heal quickly.

276
00:18:08,360 --> 00:18:09,360
But...

277
00:18:09,360 --> 00:18:11,360
Isn't that why it hurts so bad?

278
00:18:14,360 --> 00:18:15,360
I found it!

279
00:18:16,360 --> 00:18:17,360
Alright, let's begin.

280
00:18:20,360 --> 00:18:33,360
It's back on!

281
00:18:34,360 --> 00:18:37,360
But now it itches.

282
00:18:37,360 --> 00:18:39,360
Just those healing pains at work.

283
00:18:39,360 --> 00:18:42,360
Lyos, you did well.

284
00:18:42,360 --> 00:18:45,360
You really managed to slay the Red Dragon.

285
00:18:45,360 --> 00:18:50,360
Thanks to all of you, it was possible cause we each did our part.

286
00:18:51,360 --> 00:18:53,360
I felt like we weren't gonna make it at one point.

287
00:18:54,360 --> 00:18:55,360
Even I was shaking in my boots.

288
00:18:56,360 --> 00:18:58,360
Guess we underestimated it, didn't we?

289
00:18:59,360 --> 00:19:01,360
Eh, doesn't matter since we won.

290
00:19:02,360 --> 00:19:03,360
Although...

291
00:19:03,360 --> 00:19:04,360
Here, Lyos.

292
00:19:05,360 --> 00:19:06,360
Kensuke!

293
00:19:06,360 --> 00:19:08,360
I still haven't forgiven you regarding that thing yet.

294
00:19:09,360 --> 00:19:11,360
So we'll have a long talk later.

295
00:19:11,360 --> 00:19:12,360
Hmm?

296
00:19:12,360 --> 00:19:13,360
Alright.

297
00:19:14,360 --> 00:19:15,360
Okay.

298
00:19:15,360 --> 00:19:17,360
Let's go check inside of its stomach.

299
00:19:27,360 --> 00:19:28,360
Such thick skin!

300
00:19:29,360 --> 00:19:32,360
We wouldn't have even reached the fat underneath if we'd fought it with Senshi's knife.

301
00:19:33,360 --> 00:19:36,360
Which means, getting to the stomach could take us a while.

302
00:19:36,360 --> 00:19:37,360
Want me to blow it up?

303
00:19:38,360 --> 00:19:39,360
Nah.

304
00:19:39,360 --> 00:19:41,360
Dragon's organs should be similar to what other creatures have.

305
00:19:41,360 --> 00:19:44,360
So let's try to carve our way through bit by bit.

306
00:19:53,360 --> 00:19:54,360
I hit a rib bone.

307
00:19:54,360 --> 00:19:56,360
We'll have to go around it and keep on digging.

308
00:20:00,360 --> 00:20:01,360
It's dark.

309
00:20:01,360 --> 00:20:02,360
Should we light a lantern?

310
00:20:02,360 --> 00:20:03,360
No fire.

311
00:20:03,360 --> 00:20:04,360
Marcel.

312
00:20:04,360 --> 00:20:05,360
Lights, please?

313
00:20:15,360 --> 00:20:16,360
It's hot.

314
00:20:17,360 --> 00:20:20,360
Reminds me of back when I used to work in the mines.

315
00:20:22,360 --> 00:20:23,360
This is...

316
00:20:24,360 --> 00:20:25,360
The stomach!

317
00:20:28,360 --> 00:20:29,360
Right.

318
00:20:30,360 --> 00:20:31,360
Here goes.

319
00:20:33,360 --> 00:20:34,360
Empty.

320
00:20:34,360 --> 00:20:35,360
But...

321
00:20:35,360 --> 00:20:36,360
How?

322
00:20:36,360 --> 00:20:37,360
Maybe it's a different dragon?

323
00:20:37,360 --> 00:20:38,360
Not possible.

324
00:20:38,360 --> 00:20:39,360
It has the same scar above its eye as the one we saw that day.

325
00:20:40,360 --> 00:20:46,360
Male dragons are territorial, so I doubt there'd be many within the same vicinity.

326
00:20:46,360 --> 00:20:47,360
Let's check the intestines, too.

327
00:20:47,360 --> 00:20:48,360
No...

328
00:20:48,360 --> 00:20:49,360
Not even a single bone has left it there.

329
00:20:49,360 --> 00:20:50,360
I need to hurry and check his tongue.

330
00:20:50,360 --> 00:20:54,360
Maybe it digested faster because it was moving around.

331
00:20:54,360 --> 00:20:55,360
Hang on.

332
00:20:55,360 --> 00:20:56,360
Hang on.

333
00:20:56,360 --> 00:20:57,360
Here.

334
00:20:57,360 --> 00:21:10,360
Huh?

335
00:21:10,360 --> 00:21:13,580
Maybe it digested faster because it was moving around.

336
00:21:17,260 --> 00:21:18,200
Hang on.

337
00:21:38,020 --> 00:21:39,460
What is this?

338
00:21:39,460 --> 00:21:42,040
A giant clump of hair and bones.

339
00:21:42,680 --> 00:21:46,920
Animals that swallow their prey whole spit out the indigestible parts all at once.

340
00:21:48,040 --> 00:21:51,600
However, red dragons use it as fuel for their fire breath instead.

341
00:21:52,840 --> 00:21:57,460
Judging by this black fur, looks like it ate a few wargs and...

342
00:21:57,460 --> 00:22:03,680
A strand of hair! Could it be?

343
00:22:04,100 --> 00:22:07,240
Let's sort through it. We might find some human bones.

344
00:22:07,240 --> 00:22:14,200
Hey, isn't this rod...

345
00:22:14,200 --> 00:22:17,780
Laios! Look! This staff!

346
00:22:17,780 --> 00:22:26,160
Valon?

347
00:22:26,160 --> 00:22:26,200
Valon?

